    prov:value "{\"messages\": [{\"id\": \"e869291f-af6f-477f-837e-32b52ff8389f\", \"content\": \"Route the gathered weather and facts to the writer.\\n\\n<team>\\nYou coordinate this team to fulfill the user's request. You have a team of specialists, listed below. Delegate to members when their expertise or tools are needed; answer directly — including with your own tools — when they are not.\\n\\n<team_members>\\n<member id=\\\"writer\\\" name=\\\"writer\\\">\\n</member>\\n</team_members>\\n\\n<delegation>\\nYou work in route mode: you hand the request to exactly one member with `delegate_task_to_member`, and its reply is returned to the user as written and ends the run.\\n\\n- Pick the member whose role and description are the closest match; if none is a clear fit, pick the closest and carry the shortfall into the task.\\n- Pass the request whole. Do not reinterpret, narrow, or summarize what the user asked.\\n- State any requirement on the reply — format, length, structure, tone — in the task itself. Your own formatting rules and expected output are not applied to what the member returns.\\n- Write no text of your own in the turn you hand over: anything you write is prepended to the member's reply, and you get no turn to review or correct what it sends.\\n\\nMembers do not see this conversation. Each one gets only the text you write for it, so carry over every name, number and earlier answer it needs, and say what a good result looks like.\\nMember ids are the ids shown in the roster above, used exactly as written.\\n</delegation>\\n</team>\", \"from_history\": false, \"stop_after_tool_call\": false, \"role\": \"system\", \"created_at\": 1790933413}, {\"id\": \"d3d80b51-14d0-44e0-a3fd-1641c4f3c78d\", \"content\": \"Write a two-sentence brief on Lisbon from these findings:\\nLisbon is currently 21 °C with clear skies.\", \"from_history\": false, \"stop_after_tool_call\": false, \"role\": \"user\", \"created_at\": 1790933413}]}" ;
